#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:1
msgid "Unsafe GPU communication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:3
msgid ""
"The CUDA 13.5 communication surface provides peer-memory access and "
"multicast operations. Kernels use `cutile::core::*` for memory operations "
"and ordering types, and `cutile::tileir::*` for the new pointer "
"classifications and multicast operations. The host owns allocation, mapping, "
"access permissions, and lifetime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:8
msgid ""
"These are low-level unsafe APIs. They expose the synchronization primitives "
"needed to build communication protocols; they do not insert an inter-GPU "
"barrier automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:12
msgid "Unicast: access one GPU's memory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:14
msgid ""
"`unsafe ptr_with_attr_unicast(pointer)` classifies a pointer as an NVLink "
"peer pointer. It preserves the address and does not allocate memory, enable "
"peer access, or grant permission. Reshape, broadcast, and offset operations "
"preserve the classification."
msgstr ""

