#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:28
msgid ""
"Views built over a unicast pointer retain its classification and support the "
"ordinary view memory operations, subject to their type and shape "
"restrictions. The concurrent unicast example exercises pointer loads, "
"stores, and integer atomic adds; it does not claim execution coverage of "
"every atomic mode or type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:33
msgid ""
"For operations coordinating different GPUs, choose `scope::System`. Device "
"scope covers the issuing device and is insufficient for an inter-GPU release/"
"acquire handshake. Atomics require peer-native atomic support. The pointer's "
"target must be accessible to the issuing GPU for the entire launch."
msgstr ""

