#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:63
msgid ""
"Rust `u64` uses the same Tile IR `i64` representation as Rust `i64`; 64-bit "
"addition has the same result bits for both types and wraps modulo 2^64. "
"Integer Min/Max use signed comparisons regardless of the Rust type; use Umin/"
"Umax for unsigned comparisons. Multicast stores support i32, i64, u64, f16, "
"bf16, f32, and f64. Floating-point tiles must occupy a multiple of four "
"bytes; f16 and bf16 views additionally require exactly one statically unit-"
"stride dimension. Each true `inbounds` entry is the caller's promise that "
"the corresponding tile coordinate is valid for every program instance."
msgstr ""

