msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:82
msgid ""
"A token alone does not signal another GPU. An alias fence alone does not "
"wait for another GPU. A polling load must have the proper acquire ordering "
"and its returned token must feed dependent reads. Chain the producer's data "
"operation to its release signal as well; source-code order alone is "
"insufficient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:87
msgid ""
"For example, each GPU can write its contribution, release-store a sequence "
"number into its peer's inbox, acquire-load its own inbox until the expected "
"number arrives, and then read the contributions. A second exchange after the "
"reads prevents either producer from reusing the buffer too early. Monotonic "
"sequence numbers distinguish repeated uses of the same inbox."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:93
msgid ""
"The example includes explicit alias fences around transitions between "
"ordinary and multicast mappings. Both kernels launch before the host waits "
"for either one. A sequential pair of blocking launches would deadlock while "
"the first kernel waited for an unlaunched peer."
msgstr ""

