#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:110
msgid ""
"Query and honor allocation/multicast granularity. Add every multicast "
"participant before binding backing memory. Retain mappings, bindings and "
"buffers until every submitted kernel completes. Unmap before releasing the "
"associated virtual address reservation. The example grants both devices "
"access to each ordinary mapping; the multicast mode additionally maps the "
"multicast object. The unicast mode does not require or create a multicast "
"object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:117
msgid "Support and runnable example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:119
msgid ""
"The current Rust branch enables both classifications on `sm_100`, `sm_103`, "
"and `sm_107` with Tile IR 13.5. Unicast requires an NVLink path; multicast "
"also requires an NVLink SHARP-capable NVSwitch. The selected `tileiras` must "
"use a matching 13.5 backend. See [CUDA and Tile IR compatibility]"
"(compatibility.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:124
msgid "From `cutile-rs/`, with that toolchain activated:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:126
msgid ""
"cargo run -p cutile --example unsafe_comms -- unicast\n"
"cargo run -p cutile --example unsafe_comms -- multicast\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:131
msgid ""
"The source is `cutile/examples/unsafe_comms.rs`. An optional second argument "
"sets the round count, for example `-- unicast 1024`. This is a correctness "
"example with one CTA per GPU, not a throughput benchmark or a reusable "
"collective abstraction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:136
msgid ""
"Each mode runs 256 rounds by default and repeats with the launch order "
"reversed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:138
msgid ""
"**Unicast:** both GPUs read peer inputs, write peer outputs, and atomically "
"add into local and peer memory. The host checks every phase on both devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:140
msgid ""
"**Multicast:** both GPUs load-reduce their contributions and atomically "
"reduce into both backing allocations; the broadcast producer alternates each "
"round. The host checks every phase and both final backing allocations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/unsafe-comms.md:144
msgid ""
"The host precompiles both launches, initializes the inboxes, and poisons the "
"output snapshots. Between the first and last round, all coordination occurs "
"in the kernels. The polling loop is bounded and asserts if the peer fails to "
"signal. Unsupported hardware and execution failures are errors, not skips."
msgstr ""

